# Maintainer: Kulesha Evgeniy
pkgname=whyred-gaming
pkgver=1
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc="Optional Wine/box64 gaming stack for whyred (experimental)"
url="https://github.com/glavakartela/PKGBUILDs-whyred"
arch=('any')
license=('MIT')
depends=()
optdepends=(
	'wine-aarch64: Hangover Wine for Windows applications'
	'box64: x86_64 emulation backend for Wine'
	'mangohud: Vulkan/OpenGL performance overlay'
	'vkd3d: Direct3D 12 to Vulkan translation'
	'winetricks: install Windows runtimes and components'
)

package() {
	install -d "$pkgdir/usr/share/whyred-gaming"
	cat > "$pkgdir/usr/share/whyred-gaming/README" <<'EOF'
whyred-gaming is a discoverability meta package for the optional
Wine/box64 stack.  It is not a dependency of device-xiaomi-whyred.

Install the pieces you need explicitly:

  pacman -S wine-aarch64 box64
  pacman -S mangohud vkd3d winetricks   # optional

Known limits on whyred (Adreno 509 / Turnip a5xx MVP):

* Gamescope is not included and does not work yet.  Gamescope 3.17
  requires dynamicRendering, timelineSemaphore, scalarBlockLayout,
  nullDescriptor and bufferDeviceAddress; the a5xx bring-up does not
  provide them, so vkCreateDevice fails with
  VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT.
* DXVK/VKD3D are limited by the same missing Vulkan features.  Wine
  works through wined3d/OpenGL for older applications.
* Wine runs x86_64 Windows binaries through box64 (wowbox64.dll).
  32-bit (i386) PE support needs the i386 Wine arch and box32, which
  are not built yet.
* Performance is limited by the 4x Cortex-A73 + 4x Cortex-A53 CPU and
  3.6 GiB RAM.  Expect old or lightweight applications, not modern
  games.
EOF
}
